            <ArticleTitle>[The microsurgical anatomy of the coronary arteries and veins of the heart].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>40-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study has been carried out in 80 corpses of adults by macro-microscopic preparation and histotopographic methods. Four neurovascular bundles: right and left coronary, anterior and posterior interventricular ones have been described. Three divisions: periadventitial, perivasal and paravasal were established in perivascular part of cardiac nervous plexus. Morphometry of the coronary arteries wall layers has been performed under normal conditions and in coronarosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
